Blocking OneDrive on Standalone Workstations
In a non-domain workstation setup, OneDrive can be completely neutralized without uninstalling by combining policy suppression, process termination, UI cleanup, and execution locking.
Step 1: Enforce Local Policy Block & Terminate Process
Running the commands below configures the DisableFileSyncNGSC policy (mirroring Group Policy) and immediately stops active background syncing engines:
reg add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\OneDrive" /v DisableFileSyncNGSC /t REG_DWORD /d 1 /f
taskkill /f /im OneDrive.exe
Optional — Prevent pre-login network traffic:
reg add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\OneDrive" /v PreventNetworkTrafficPreUserSignIn /t REG_DWORD /d 1 /f
Step 2: Remove OneDrive from File Explorer Navigation Pane
To ensure the OneDrive folder does not clutter the left-hand directory tree in File Explorer:
64-bit Systems (Standard):
reg add "HKCR\CLSID\{018D5C66-4533-4307-9B53-224DE2ED1FE6}" /v System.IsPinnedToNameSpaceTree /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f
32-bit Applications on 64-bit OS (WOW6432Node):
reg add "HKCR\WOW6432Node\CLSID\{018D5C66-4533-4307-9B53-224DE2ED1FE6}" /v System.IsPinnedToNameSpaceTree /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f
Step 3: Remove Auto-Start Entry & Hard-Block Binary
To prevent OneDrive from initiating upon user logon and block direct execution:
Remove Run on Startup Entry:
reg delete "HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run" /v OneDrive /f
Hard-Block OneDrive.exe Execution (IFEO):
reg add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Image File Execution Options\OneDrive.exe" /v Debugger /t REG_SZ /d "systray.exe" /f
Step 4: Full Restoration / Re-enabling Procedure
To restore full OneDrive functionality on the workstation at any future point:
reg delete "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\OneDrive" /v DisableFileSyncNGSC /f
reg delete "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Image File Execution Options\OneDrive.exe" /f
reg add "HKCR\CLSID\{018D5C66-4533-4307-9B53-224DE2ED1FE6}" /v System.IsPinnedToNameSpaceTree /t REG_DWORD /d 1 /f
reg add "HKCR\WOW6432Node\CLSID\{018D5C66-4533-4307-9B53-224DE2ED1FE6}" /v System.IsPinnedToNameSpaceTree /t REG_DWORD /d 1 /f
